  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186068695,
      "id": "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c",
      "title": "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/ff8685d53e8103c29c06dcebef4d21c94fbbad077d685fbbe9ceed389d6735f8.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-3$\n\n- **II.** $x=0$\n\n- **III.** $x=2$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $-3.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-3$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0.$ Since there is a jump at $x=0,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of  $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"I and III only\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/ad93e1bddb322a144349f3cf462fe6b0a10b3e954bf47489e9d65f6320dc33cb.png)",
