  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186068695,
      "id": "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c",
      "title": "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/bb29ffc31a74b2a77e96ef4fddecb9808f341187f0c90bc8472b1f2b1909269a.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-8$\n\n- **II.** $x=-2$\n\n- **III.** $x=2$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $-8.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-8$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-2.$ Since there is a jump at $x=-2,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of  $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"I and III only\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/c3dca70ab2aa53d1914b5e3bf40036f361b19ba1adbeb8f371077051ffbe8c24.png)",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false",
