  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186068695,
      "id": "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c",
      "title": "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/45e213da7a7cbcf8b6e7f662eac9854fe41c4ce690a7c934e7632fe023cc7fec.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=2$\n\n- **II.** $x=5$\n\n- **III.** $x=7$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $2.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=5.$ Since there is a jump at $x=5,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=5$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=7.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of  $x=7$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"I and III only\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/61a26cdd02cfd7bc087c9a9cbb58caf794f474ff05fb7713a66dcc5a24d2471e.png)",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
